        -:   51:/*Width-correct libm for NV.
        -:   52:
        -:   53:C has no type-generic <math.h>: sqrt(), log(), lgamma() and the rest are
        -:   54:declared to take a double, so calling them with an NV on a long-double or
        -:   55:__float128 build converts the argument down to double, computes at double
        -:   56:precision and converts back. Nothing warns, nothing fails to compile, and the
        -:   57:result looks entirely plausible -- it is simply carrying 53 bits of mantissa on
        -:   58:a perl built for 64 or 113. Measured on perl-5.12.5 (long double) before this
        -:   59:layer existed, sd(1..5) came back as exactly the double-rounded sqrt(2.5),
        -:   60:9.5e-17 away from the long-double value perl's own sqrt() gives.
        -:   61:
        -:   62:So every NV-valued libm call in this file goes through the nv_* macros below,
        -:   63:which paste on the suffix for the width NV actually is: none for double, `l`
        -:   64:for long double, `q` for __float128 (perl.h has already included <quadmath.h>
        -:   65:by this point, and the quadmath perl's $Config{perllibs} already carries
        -:   66:-lquadmath, so the q functions need nothing extra at link time).
        -:   67:
        -:   68:The long-double row is conditional because the `l` variants are C99 but not
        -:   69:universally present -- some BSD libms are thin on them. Makefile.PL link-tests
        -:   70:the whole set and defines LIKER_HAVE_LONG_DOUBLE_MATH only when every one of
        -:   71:them resolves; without it this falls back to the double functions, which is
        -:   72:exactly what the code did before and so cannot be a regression.
        -:   73:
        -:   74:Float classification -- NaN, infinite, finite -- is nv_isnan()/nv_isinf()/
        -:   75:nv_isfinite() below, and neither the C99 macros nor perl's Perl_isnan /
        -:   76:Perl_isinf / Perl_isfinite may be used in this file. See the comment on
        -:   77:those three.*/
        -:   78:#if defined(USE_QUADMATH)
        -:   79:#  define LIKER_NVFN(base) base ## q
        -:   80:#elif defined(USE_LONG_DOUBLE) && defined(LIKER_HAVE_LONG_DOUBLE_MATH)
        -:   81:#  define LIKER_NVFN(base) base ## l
        -:   82:#else
        -:   83:#  define LIKER_NVFN(base) base
        -:   84:#endif
