        -: 1439:/*General R x C exact test (used for anything that is not 2x2)
        -: 1440:
        -: 1441:The 2x2 machinery above cannot describe larger tables, so the R x C case
        -: 1442:is handled by direct enumeration of every contingency table that shares
        -: 1443:the observed row and column margins.  Under the null the probability of a
        -: 1444:table T with fixed margins is the multivariate hypergeometric
        -: 1445:
        -: 1446:     P(T) = (prod_i R_i!)(prod_j C_j!) / ( N! prod_ij t_ij! )
        -: 1447:
        -: 1448:The (two-sided) p-value is the sum of P(T) over all such T whose
        -: 1449:probability is <= P(observed).  Only two-sided is defined for R x C, so
        -: 1450:'alternative' is ignored for larger tables (matching R's fisher.test).*/
