        -: 8036:/*anova() : sequential (Type-I) ANOVA table for a linear model, returned in
        -: 8037:          the same shape as aov() in this module, OR an F-test comparison
        -: 8038:          of two or more nested models (R's anova(m1, m2, ...) generic).
        -: 8039:
        -: 8040:  my $tab = anova(\%data, 'yield ~ ctrl');            # one model  -> HashRef
        -: 8041:  my $tab = anova(\%data, 'len ~ supp * dose');       # one model  -> HashRef
        -: 8042:  my $cmp = anova(\%data, 'y ~ a', 'y ~ a + b');      # 2+ models  -> ArrayRef
        -: 8043:
        -: 8044:---- single-model form (one formula) --
        -: 8045:Input mirrors aov(): a Hash-of-Arrays (\%h, columns) or Array-of-Hashes
        -: 8046:(\@a, rows), plus a formula string 'response ~ rhs'. The RHS understands
        -: 8047:'+', ':' (interaction) and '*' (factorial expansion: a*b -> a + b + a:b,
        -: 8048:a*b*c -> a + b + c + a:b + a:c + b:c + a:b:c). Bare string columns are
        -: 8049:treated as factors and treatment-coded (first level = reference); numeric
        -: 8050:columns and I(x^2) enter as single regressors. Interactions form the
        -: 8051:product of their factors' coded columns, so factor:factor uses
        -: 8052:(la-1)*(lb-1) columns exactly as R's treatment contrasts do.
        -: 8053:
        -: 8054:The model is fit sequentially by Householder QR (apply_householder_aov)
        -: 8055:and the model SS is decomposed term by term, in formula order (Type I).
        -: 8056:Collinear / rank-deficient terms gracefully receive 0 df and 0 Sum Sq.
        -: 8057:Rows with any missing / non-numeric response or predictor are dropped
        -: 8058:listwise (R's default na.omit).
        -: 8059:
        -: 8060:Returns a HashRef keyed by term name (plus "Residuals"); each value is a
        -: 8061:nested hash using R's column names:
        -: 8062:    term        => { Df, "Sum Sq", "Mean Sq", "F value", "Pr(>F)" }
        -: 8063:    Residuals   => { Df, "Sum Sq", "Mean Sq" }
        -: 8064:"Mean Sq"/"F value"/"Pr(>F)" are omitted where undefined (0-df terms; the
        -: 8065:Residuals row never carries an F test), matching aov()'s output.
        -: 8066:
        -: 8067:---- model-comparison form (two or more formulas) -------------------------
        -: 8068:anova(\%data, 'y ~ a', 'y ~ a + b', ...) fits every model and returns an
        -: 8069:ArrayRef with one HashRef per model, in the order supplied, mirroring R's
        -: 8070:anova(m1, m2, ...) table (columns Res.Df, RSS, Df, Sum of Sq, F, Pr(>F)):
        -: 8071:    [ { "Res.Df", "RSS", formula },
        -: 8072:      { "Res.Df", "RSS", "Df", "Sum of Sq", "F", "Pr(>F)", formula }, ... ]
        -: 8073:The first row carries no comparison stats (nothing precedes it). For each
        -: 8074:later row: Df = drop in residual df from the previous model, "Sum of Sq" =
        -: 8075:drop in RSS, and F = ("Sum of Sq"/Df) / scale, where scale is the residual
        -: 8076:mean square of the *largest* model in the set (smallest residual df) --
        -: 8077:the common denominator R uses for the whole table. "F"/"Pr(>F)" are omitted
        -: 8078:for any row whose Df is not positive (non-nested / equal-size steps).
        -: 8079:
        -: 8080:All models are fit on ONE shared row set: completeness is evaluated
